<article class="prose">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>I'm a full-stack software developer with nearly 20 years of experience building
  websites and applications. The day my family got internet access I learned how to
  "program HTML" and never looked back.</p>

  <p>My career started when a few high school friends and I launched a web development
  company aimed at local small businesses. Over the two decades since I've worked in
  Javascript, .NET, C++, Java, PHP, Ruby, Python, and Go, plus more frameworks and
  libraries than I care to count.</p>

  <p>The last few years have found me leading a team of young developers on a monolithic
  application. The daily challenge is finding ways to make myself and my teammates grow
  as developers and as people.</p>

  <h2>Learning next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://elixir-lang.org/">Elixir</a> — I've wanted a functional language
    in my toolset for a while. I played with <a href="https://www.haskell.org/">Haskell</a>
    previously, but Elixir has a serious web framework in
    <a href="https://phoenixframework.org/">Phoenix</a> and a larger local community.</li>
    <li><a href="https://graphql.org/">GraphQL</a> — an API layer that does a good job of
    stitching together data across services.</li>
  </ul>

